{"event": "tool_call", "t": 1795207426.145, "name": "report", "arguments": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "rpt_category_performance", "summary": "The model drove from products and left-joined down to variants and order lines. Every product with no sales therefore produced a row with a NULL sales_month, and those rows counted never-sold products in unique_products (for example 132 PHYSICAL products under a NULL month with 0 orders). That inflated the product counts and added junk rows to a monthly report. Rebasing the model on order lines, the grain of sales, leaves revenue, units and gross profit unchanged and removes the phantom rows."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "diff", "ref": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "finding": "Original FROM products p LEFT JOIN variants LEFT JOIN order_lines, so products without any order lines formed rows with NULL sales_month. Before the fix the mart had 202 rows, including NULL-month rows for DIGITAL, GIFT_CARD, PHYSICAL and SERVICE."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.stg_orders__order_lines vs main.rpt_category_performance", "finding": "Source line_total sum is 722,313.24 across 3,576 lines. The original mart revenue was also 722,313.24, so no revenue was lost by the join. Units were 6,590 in both."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "source reconciliation after fix", "finding": "Mart revenue 722,313.24, units 6,590, gross profit 608,293.75. Source gross profit (line_total minus quantity times variant cost_price) is 608,293.75, so these match."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.rpt_category_performance NULL sales_month rows", "finding": "Only the PHYSICAL NULL-month row remains, with 18 lines, revenue 2,950.78 and 0 orders. Those lines reference ORPHAN-ORD order_ids that are missing from the orders source. This is a bad-source-data issue and is outside the model's lineage."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.stg_product__product_variants", "finding": "variant_id is unique (1,266 rows), product_id is unique in products (487 rows), and order_line_id and order_id are unique, so the joins do not fan out."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "summary": "Changed the driving table from products to order_lines, and left-joined variants, products and orders from the lines. Output columns, grain (category x sales_month), and materialisation are unchanged. Totals reconcile to source; products with no sales no longer create NULL-month rows or inflate unique_products."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "duration_s": 225.34, "output_chars": 104, "is_error": false}
