{"event": "report", "t": 1795207614.101, "claim": "fixed", "verdict": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "rpt_category_performance", "summary": "The model drove from products and left-joined down to variants and order lines. Every product with no sales therefore produced a row with a NULL sales_month, and those rows counted never-sold products in unique_products (for example 132 PHYSICAL products under a NULL month with 0 orders). That inflated the product counts and added junk rows to a monthly report. Rebasing the model on order lines, the grain of sales, leaves revenue, units and gross profit unchanged and removes the phantom rows."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "diff", "ref": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "finding": "Original FROM products p LEFT JOIN variants LEFT JOIN order_lines, so products without any order lines formed rows with NULL sales_month. Before the fix the mart had 202 rows, including NULL-month rows for DIGITAL, GIFT_CARD, PHYSICAL and SERVICE."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.stg_orders__order_lines vs main.rpt_category_performance", "finding": "Source line_total sum is 722,313.24 across 3,576 lines. The original mart revenue was also 722,313.24, so no revenue was lost by the join. Units were 6,590 in both."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "source reconciliation after fix", "finding": "Mart revenue 722,313.24, units 6,590, gross profit 608,293.75. Source gross profit (line_total minus quantity times variant cost_price) is 608,293.75, so these match."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.rpt_category_performance NULL sales_month rows", "finding": "Only the PHYSICAL NULL-month row remains, with 18 lines, revenue 2,950.78 and 0 orders. Those lines reference ORPHAN-ORD order_ids that are missing from the orders source. This is a bad-source-data issue and is outside the model's lineage."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.stg_product__product_variants", "finding": "variant_id is unique (1,266 rows), product_id is unique in products (487 rows), and order_line_id and order_id are unique, so the joins do not fan out."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "summary": "Changed the driving table from products to order_lines, and left-joined variants, products and orders from the lines. Output columns, grain (category x sales_month), and materialisation are unchanged. Totals reconcile to source; products with no sales no longer create NULL-month rows or inflate unique_products."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "diffs": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n@@ -26,8 +26,8 @@\n     sum(ol.line_total) as revenue,\n     avg(ol.unit_price) as avg_unit_price,\n     sum(ol.line_total) - sum(ol.quantity_ordered * pv.cost_price) as gross_profit\n-from products p\n-left join product_variants pv on p.product_id = pv.product_id\n-left join order_lines ol on pv.variant_id = ol.variant_id\n+from order_lines ol\n+left join product_variants pv on ol.variant_id = pv.variant_id\n+left join products p on pv.product_id = p.product_id\n left join orders o on ol.order_id = o.order_id\n group by 1, 2\n"}], "text": "model started from `products` and left-joined down to variants and order lines. Every product with no sales therefore produced a row with a NULL `sales_month`. Those rows counted never-sold products in `unique_products`; for example, 132 PHYSICAL products sat under a NULL month with 0 orders. This inflated the product counts and added junk rows to a monthly report.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the driving table to `order_lines`, the grain of sales, and left-joined variants, products and orders from it. Output columns, the category \u00d7 month grain and the materialisation are unchanged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Source line totals are 722,313.24 across 3,576 lines. The original mart revenue was the same, so the old join lost no revenue. The bad part was the phantom rows.\n- After the fix the mart has 199 rows, down from 202. Revenue is 722,313.24, units 6,590 and gross profit 608,293.75. Source gross profit (line total minus quantity \u00d7 variant cost) is also 608,293.75.\n- Variant, product and order keys are unique, so the joins don't fan out.\n\n**Open issue, not fixed:** 18 order lines (revenue 2,950.78) reference `ORPHAN-ORD-*` order IDs that are missing from the orders source. They land in a single PHYSICAL row with a NULL `sales_month`. This is bad source data outside the model's lineage, and I did not filter it out because that would drop revenue.\n\n**Other failures, not touched:** The build still reports about 122 failing tests, mostly not-null and unique tests on `stg_ga__*` and `stg_legacy__*` staging models. There is also a seed error: `product_categories` clashes with an existing `PRODUCT_CATEGORIES` relation. None of these are in this model's lineage, and I could not fix them without changing tests or upstream staging, which the rules forbid.\n\n**Confidence:** medium. The reconciliation checks pass, but the intended treatment of CREDIT and RETURNED lines in revenue was not something I could confirm from the code.\n\n**Changed file:** `models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql`"}
